# What the line reader saw and the parse must too. A held name sent to a
# constant names the constant, whatever its shape (Settings, a writer;
# Widget, held then maybe replaced). An unrun `method("on_#{e}")` sends a
# shape (Bus). A literal in a string of code that an interpolation spells
# part of is computed (Target). A symbol sent where the typing finds no
# call keeps saying it is not read as one (Host, sent from a module), and
# `public_send` runs no private or protected method (Secret, Guarded).
# Each send of a chain is its own (Chained), and a name sent twice says so
# of the one not read as a call (Twice).
dead app Settings#timeout==unreferenced~sent Widget#other_b=unreferenced~Widget Bus#on_start=unreferenced~on_* Target#list_a=unreferenced~Target Host#hook=convention-only~:hook Secret#hidden=convention-only~:hidden Chained#aaa=single-caller Twice#b1=single-caller~:b1 Guarded#shielded=convention-only~:shielded
